    <div class="update-entry">
    <p class="update-date">05-29-2026</p>
    <div class="update-content"><p><strong>Viewer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><p>Layer system revamped (again).</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Fixes <a href="https://github.com/skuqre/nkas-issues/issues/4">nkas-issues#4</a></p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>FOR USC USERS: Exported USC layers will not work for now; this new layer system is already implemented for v1.7.0, but no migration is implemented.</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p>Added Bulk Edit!</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="update-entry">
    <p class="update-date">05-29-2026</p>
    <div class="update-content"><p><strong>Viewer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><p>Removed the higher quality scales.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Out of people&#39;s curiosity, they will try what 8x and 16x are. They were added out of fun, really.</p>
</li>
<li><p>What Quality Scale does is change to a higher render size relative to your screen&#39;s resolution.</p>
</li>
<li><p>So 2x is <strong>twice</strong> the screen size, 1x is just the screen size, and so on...</p>
</li>
<li><p>Now ask yourself what setting it to 16x does...</p>
</li>
<li><p>Oh right, this also resets the setting.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="update-entry">
    <p class="update-date">05-29-2026</p>
    <div class="update-content"><p><strong>Viewer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><p>Filters have been added! You can now easily investigate for veins in the Viewer.</p>
<ul>
<li>Duly note that this does not affect exporting, so when you export images/gifs, they will look normal.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p>GIF Exporting has been massively improved with FFmpeg!</p>
<ul>
<li><p>I don&#39;t know if people want advanced settings for this, but if you do, tell me through <a href="https://github.com/skuqre/nkas-issues/issues">nkas-issues</a> or the <a href="/feedback/">Feedback Form</a>.</p>
</li>
<li><p>But if you do want higher control for now, consider using the &quot;Download as Frames&quot; option and using FFmpeg with those instead.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><p>For exports with framerates, you can now set a custom framerate.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
    </div>
    
